WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.510
In ammonia, nitrogen has an
oxidation state of minus three.

2
00:00:04.560 --> 00:00:09.290
In nitric acid, nitrogen has an
oxidation state of plus five.

3
00:00:09.340 --> 00:00:11.550
It's the same element in both.

4
00:00:11.600 --> 00:00:16.950
So how can nitrogen be minus three in
ammonia, but plus five in nitric acid?

5
00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:20.970
In this mission, you'll find out
what an oxidation state really is,

6
00:00:21.020 --> 00:00:23.590
and learn the rules for assigning one.

7
00:00:23.640 --> 00:00:26.530
You'll work out oxidation
states in molecules and ions,

8
00:00:26.580 --> 00:00:31.510
and use them to name compounds,
such as potassium manganate seven.

9
00:00:31.560 --> 00:00:36.600
Your mission: explain how one element
can have such different oxidation states.
